<!--
  Android 17 overlay on the stock AOSP android-17.0.0_r1 manifest.

  NO PROJECTS LEFT. This file is deliberately empty rather than deleted, and both halves of that
  are on purpose.

  Empty, because A17 now syncs stock AOSP and nothing else. The last entry here was
  the upstream prebuilts project, tracking its master branch for the Mesa drivers and their
  dependency closure; R3 (bd remora-ykhz) retired it by building Mesa from source, and
  bd remora-28ix.4 removed the project and the upstream remote from both this file and
  pinned-manifest-a17.xml. The header that used to stand here said "when it goes, this file goes" —
  the first half happened, the second half turned out to be wrong, which is the next paragraph.

  Not deleted, because the engine requires it to exist. SourceBuild.cpp's unpinned path does
  `cp <source-build>/local_manifests/remora-a<ver>*.xml .repo/local_manifests/` and Chain.cpp
  preflights the glob, so removing the file breaks unpinned A17 builds with a missing-manifest
  error rather than doing nothing. An overlay with no projects IS the correct A17 overlay, and it
  costs nothing to keep: repo reads it, adds nothing, and the tree is stock AOSP plus the staged
  Remora trees. Keep it in step with pinned-manifest-a17.xml — that one is the reproducible pin,
  this is the tip-tracking overlay, and a project present in only one of them makes the build
  depend on which manifest was used.

  Everything Remora authors — device/remora, vendor/remora, hardware/remora/c2-va — is
  deliberately NOT a project here and never was. It is vendored under vendor/source-build/ and
  staged into the tree before lunch. No manifest can provide Remora-authored source, and pointing
  a remote at one machine's disk made the build unreproducible everywhere else (bd remora-28ix.4).

  The upstream device tree and its OMX and c2 components were removed in R2c (bd
  remora-28ix.4): A17 lunches the staged device/remora, the codec2 wiring is absorbed into
  vendor/remora, and the OMX plugin gated on a boot arg Remora never emitted.

  Base tree:  repo init -u https://android.googlesource.com/platform/manifest -b android-17.0.0_r1
  Lunch:      remora_x86_64-cp2a-userdebug
  See bead remora-cbd.
-->
<manifest>
</manifest>
